},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"config","children":[{"type":"text","value":"config"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PacedMutationsConfig.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PacedMutationsConfig"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration including onMutate, mutationFn and strategy"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that accepts variables and returns a Transaction"}]},{"type":"code","value":"(variables): Transaction<T>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/Transaction.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Transaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Debounced mutations for auto-save\nconst updateTodo = createPacedMutations<string>({\n  onMutate: (text) => {\n    // Apply optimistic update immediately\n    collection.update(id, draft => { draft.text = text })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: debounceStrategy({ wait: 500 })\n})\n\n// Call with variables, returns a transaction\nconst tx = updateTodo('New text')\n\n// Await persistence or handle errors\nawait tx.when('settled')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"// Queue strategy for sequential processing\nconst addTodo = createPacedMutations<{ text: string }>({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    collection.insert({ id: uuid(), text, completed: false })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'front'\n  })\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvariables","text":"TVariables","level":3},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"config","text":"config","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"variables","text":"variables","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createPacedMutations<TVariables, T>(config): (variables) => Transaction<T>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/paced-mutations.ts:93](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/paced-mutations.ts#L93)\n\nCreates a paced mutations manager with pluggable timing strategies.\n\nThis function provides a way to control when and how optimistic mutations\nare persisted to the backend, using strategies like debouncing, queuing,\nor throttling. The optimistic updates are applied immediately via `onMutate`,\nand the actual persistence is controlled by the strategy.\n\nThe returned function accepts variables of type TVariables and returns a\nTransaction object that can be awaited to know when persistence completes\nor to handle errors.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TVariables\n\n`TVariables` = `unknown`\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* `object` = `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\n## Parameters\n\n### config\n\n[`PacedMutationsConfig`](../interfaces/PacedMutationsConfig.md)\\<`TVariables`, `T`\\>\n\nConfiguration including onMutate, mutationFn and strategy\n\n## Returns\n\nA function that accepts variables and returns a Transaction\n\n```ts\n(variables): Transaction<T>;\n```\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### variables\n\n`TVariables`\n\n### Returns\n\n[`Transaction`](../interfaces/Transaction.md)\\<`T`\\>\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\n// Debounced mutations for auto-save\nconst updateTodo = createPacedMutations<string>({\n  onMutate: (text) => {\n    // Apply optimistic update immediately\n    collection.update(id, draft => { draft.text = text })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: debounceStrategy({ wait: 500 })\n})\n\n// Call with variables, returns a transaction\nconst tx = updateTodo('New text')\n\n// Await persistence or handle errors\nawait tx.when('settled')\n```\n\n```ts\n// Queue strategy for sequential processing\nconst addTodo = createPacedMutations<{ text: string }>({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    collection.insert({ id: uuid(), text, completed: false })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'front'\n  })\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createPacedMutations\ntitle: createPacedMutations\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createPacedMutations<TVariables, T>(config): (variables) => Transaction<T>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/paced-mutations.ts:93](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/paced-mutations.ts#L93)\n\nCreates a paced mutations manager with pluggable timing strategies.\n\nThis function provides a way to control when and how optimistic mutations\nare persisted to the backend, using strategies like debouncing, queuing,\nor throttling. The optimistic updates are applied immediately via `onMutate`,\nand the actual persistence is controlled by the strategy.\n\nThe returned function accepts variables of type TVariables and returns a\nTransaction object that can be awaited to know when persistence completes\nor to handle errors.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TVariables\n\n`TVariables` = `unknown`\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* `object` = `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\n## Parameters\n\n### config\n\n[`PacedMutationsConfig`](../interfaces/PacedMutationsConfig.md)\\<`TVariables`, `T`\\>\n\nConfiguration including onMutate, mutationFn and strategy\n\n## Returns\n\nA function that accepts variables and returns a Transaction\n\n```ts\n(variables): Transaction<T>;\n```\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### variables\n\n`TVariables`\n\n### Returns\n\n[`Transaction`](../interfaces/Transaction.md)\\<`T`\\>\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\n// Debounced mutations for auto-save\nconst updateTodo = createPacedMutations<string>({\n  onMutate: (text) => {\n    // Apply optimistic update immediately\n    collection.update(id, draft => { draft.text = text })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: debounceStrategy({ wait: 500 })\n})\n\n// Call with variables, returns a transaction\nconst tx = updateTodo('New text')\n\n// Await persistence or handle errors\nawait tx.when('settled')\n```\n\n```ts\n// Queue strategy for sequential processing\nconst addTodo = createPacedMutations<{ text: string }>({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    collection.insert({ id: uuid(), text, completed: false })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: queueStrategy({\n    wait: 200,\n    addItemsTo: 'back',\n    getItemsFrom: 'front'\n  })\n})\n```\n"}
